377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Every Helm release has a history of revisions. A revision is used to track the values, Kubernetes resources, and the chart version that were used in a particular release version. A new revision is created when a chart is installed, upgraded, or rolled back. Revision data is saved in Kubernetes Secrets by default \(other options are ConfigMaps, local memory, or a PostgreSQL database, as determined by the HELM_DRIVER environment variable\). This allows your Helm release to be managed and interacted with by different users on the Kubernetes cluster.)
/E (Every Helm release has a history of revisions. A revision is used to track the values, Kubernetes resources, and the chart version that were used in a particular release version. A new revision is created when a chart is installed, upgraded, or rolled back. Revision data is saved in Kubernetes Secrets by default \(other options are ConfigMaps, local memory, or a PostgreSQL database, as determined by the HELM_DRIVER environment variable\). This allows your Helm release to be managed and interacted with by different users on the Kubernetes cluster.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
